HomelabAPI CHANGELOG
====================
Unreleased
- Added a Dependabot config (.github/dependabot.yml) that checks the
  pinned Python packages in requirements.txt monthly, waits 7 days
  after a new release, and groups all updates into one pull request

v0.10.0     2026-10-12
- Upgraded to Python 3.14 (from 3.10), FastAPI 0.143 (from 0.85),
  Pydantic 2 (from 1), and uvicorn 0.54 (from 0.18), as Python 3.10
  reaches end of life in October 2026. Python 3.10 still works for
  self-built images (checked on amd64 for this release only)
- Updated the bundled Swagger UI to 5.33.2 and ReDoc to 2.5.4, which
  are needed to show the OpenAPI 3.1 document FastAPI now produces
  (it was OpenAPI 3.0)
- Pinned every installed package in requirements.txt, so an image
  built from a release tag installs exactly what was tested
- Removed the unused aiofiles and gjcode packages
- Kept numbers sent to text fields (such as "priority": 1) and null
  sent to optional fields working as before
- Changed validation errors (HTTP 422) to Pydantic 2's format, such as
  "type": "missing" and "msg": "Field required" instead of
  "value_error.missing" and "field required", with the submitted input
  included
- Changed a true or false sent to a text field, such as
  "priority": true, to be rejected with a 422 instead of becoming
  "True" or "False"
- Updated CLAUDE.md for the new stack
- Updated ACR.md to describe the upgrade (the rating stays B1b)

v0.9.0      2026-10-10
- Changed a wrong API key to return HTTP status 401 instead of 200
  (the response body is unchanged), so tools that check the status
  code now see the failure
- Added ssl (usually port 465) and none as email protocols, alongside
  tls; an unknown protocol is now logged as a failed output instead of
  silently sending nothing
- Fixed the email output never closing its connection, and made the
  login optional for mail relays that don't need one
- Fixed outputs in current_outputs being skipped when there are
  spaces around the names, such as "telegram, email"

v0.8.1      2026-10-10
- Fixed Telegram rejecting messages that contain <, >, or & by
  escaping them before sending
- Fixed one failing output stopping the remaining outputs from being
  sent; failures are now logged with the output name and error type
- Added the missing Matrix token setting to config.yaml.sample
- Removed an incorrect note from CLAUDE.md that said /sonarr always
  fails

v0.8.0      2026-10-10
- Added URL parameter support to the default /input endpoint (#5)
- Fixed the webhook output for /input, which was passed a method
  instead of the request body
- Fixed the webhook output for /healthchecks, /monit, /smokeping, and
  /uptimerobot sending a JSON-encoded string instead of a JSON object
- Stopped the webhook output forwarding the HomelabAPI API key
- Added CLAUDE.md with run, architecture, and release notes
- Updated copyright notices to 2023-2026
- Removed deprecated version key from docker-compose.yml.sample
- Updated ACR.md to B1b for the first AI-written code

v0.7.0      2023-08-27
- Added Subject and URL support to Matrix room output

v0.6.1      2023-08-15
- Fixed Matrix room output support

v0.6.0      2023-08-15
- Added output support for Matrix rooms

v0.5.0      2023-01-06
- Added output support for ntfy.sh
- Migrated to new official HomelabAPI docker image

v0.4.0      2023-01-06
- Added output support for Gotify

v0.3.0      2023-01-06
- Added output support for Discord

v0.2.0      2023-01-05
